d3d11, winemetal: Drop draws and dispatches whose pipeline failed to compile.

When a graphics, geometry, tessellation or compute pipeline failed to compile, the context gave
the encoder no pipeline at all and encoded the draws and dispatches anyway. They then ran with
the pipeline the encoder had before, with the wrong shaders and bindings, or with none, which
faults on the GPU.

The context now sets "no pipeline" in that case, and winemetal drops the draws and dispatches
that follow until a pipeline is set again. Passes DXMT encodes in the middle of a game's draws
(the pre-raster and tile barriers) set the game's pipeline again afterwards, and now set "no
pipeline" again too when that is what the game's last pipeline was (last_pso_failed). A failed
pipeline costs the draws that use it, not the frame.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 to 0007.
Written with an AI assistant (Claude). DXMT does not accept contributions made or
co-authored by AI (its CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be sent to it as a pull
request. What was found may be reported to its developers, for them to write their own fix;
this patch leaves here when the pinned commit has one.
